# 9. Paired Scaffold-Cluster Bootstrap Definition

The headline test comparison uses a **paired scaffold-cluster bootstrap**.

## 9.1 Clustering unit

The resampling unit is the **frozen scaffold/analog cluster**, not the individual compound.

The frozen cluster-assignment artifact is:

`cyp/artifacts/cyp_baseline/cluster_assignments.csv`

SHA-256:

`4923d31401cc4f775e89377665ba0b15102245cca252911fd02e50879d10ffb8`

## 9.2 Resampling procedure

The paired cluster-bootstrap:

1. takes the frozen scaffold-cluster assignments;
2. resamples clusters **with replacement**;
3. uses the exact same resampled cluster multiset for both variants within each bootstrap draw;
4. computes the paired stock-vs-task-balanced difference for that draw;
5. repeats the procedure to obtain the bootstrap distribution of the C0 test gain.

Individual compounds are **never** resampled independently.

Resampling compounds independently would treat correlated compounds within a scaffold cluster as independent observations and would understate the width of the uncertainty interval.

The frozen cluster assignments therefore define the bootstrap clustering unit and preserve the dependence structure induced by the analog/scaffold split.

## 9.3 Bootstrap size and RNG

The bootstrap uses:

- `B = 10,000` resamples.
- Sampling with replacement at the frozen scaffold-cluster level.
- Paired resampling: stock and task-balanced use the same resampled clusters in every draw.
- Dedicated analysis RNG seed: **`20261008`**.
- Individual compounds are never independently resampled.

The dedicated analysis seed is used only for the bootstrap shuffler and is independent of the five training seeds.

## 9.4 Bootstrap statistic

Define the C0 test gain as:

$$
\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}
=
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{stock,test}}
-
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{TB,test}}
$$

Positive values favor task-balanced.

For bootstrap draw $b$:

$$
\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}^{*(b)}
=
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{stock}}^{*(b)}
-
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{TB}}^{*(b)}
$$

for $b = 1, \ldots, 10{,}000$.

The 95% percentile bootstrap interval is:

$$
\left[
Q_{0.025}\!\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}^*\right),
Q_{0.975}\!\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}^*\right)
\right]
$$

The lower confidence bound is:

$$
LCB(\Delta_{\mathrm{test}})
=
Q_{0.025}\!\left(\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}^*\right)
$$

