# 10. Frozen Headline Decision Rule

Define:

$$
\Delta_{\mathrm{test}}
=
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{stock,test}}
-
\mathrm{ST\!\!-\!RAE}_{\mathrm{TB,test}}
$$

Positive `Delta_test` favors task-balanced.

Let:

- `LCB(Delta_test)` = lower bound of the 95% paired scaffold-cluster bootstrap interval for the C0 test gain.
- `SD_seed` = sample standard deviation of the five paired C0 validation gains across the five training seeds.

### Frozen materiality rule

> **Task-balanced takes the C0 headline if and only if the lower bound of the 95% paired scaffold-cluster bootstrap interval for the test gain exceeds the measured seed-level SD. Otherwise, stock remains the headline.**

Operational criterion:

$$
LCB(\Delta_{\mathrm{test}})
>
SD_{\mathrm{seed}}
$$

is the sole headline win criterion.

This criterion incorporates both statistical separation and materiality:

- a lower bound exceeding a positive seed-noise SD necessarily excludes zero;
- the apparent improvement must also exceed the empirically measured scale of stochastic seed variation;
- no arbitrary numerical effect-size threshold is introduced.

The challenger therefore bears the burden of demonstrating a test advantage larger than measured stochastic noise.

This rule is frozen **before any held-out test number is observed**.

